   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "How to explore",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Nomas Explore\n\n1. **Queue once** (or press *New world*) to generate the opening turn from the prompt on the left.\n2. **Click the viewer**, then hold **W A S D** (move / strafe) and the **arrow keys** (turn), or **drag** with the mouse. Recording starts on the first key and runs for the turn length; **Space/Enter** ends it early. The move is queued automatically.\n3. **Text turn**: type a *change* (\"a wooden bridge crosses a stream ahead\") and/or an *action*, then press *Text turn* (or record a move: the text is used with it). They clear after use.\n4. **Undo** drops the last turn, **New world** starts over.\n\nOnly the direction and the relative speed of a move reach the model; turning speed matters (the model scales it 2.5x).\n\nThe world lives in the server's memory per viewer session. *turn_frames* holds the latest turn, *latent* the whole world (VAE Decode it for the full video)."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## Nomas Explore\n\n1. **Queue once** (or press *New world*) to generate the opening turn from the prompt on the left.\n2. **Click the viewer**, then hold **W A S D** (move / strafe) and the **arrow keys** (turn), or **drag** with the mouse. Recording starts on the first key and runs for the turn length; **Space/Enter** ends it early. The move is queued automatically.\n3. **Text turn**: type a *change* (\"a wooden bridge crosses a stream ahead\") and/or an *action*, then press *Text turn* (or record a move: the text is used with it). They clear after use.\n4. **Undo** drops the last turn, **New world** starts over.\n\nOnly the direction and the relative speed of a move reach the model; turning speed matters (the model scales it 2.5x).\n\nThe world lives in the server's memory per viewer session. *turn_frames* holds the latest turn, *latent* the whole world (VAE Decode it for the full video)."
   },
